---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import QuickAnswer from "../components/QuickAnswer.astro";
import MoreInCategory from "../components/MoreInCategory.astro";
import { authorSchema, authorName } from "../data/authors";
import AuthorAvatar from "../components/AuthorAvatar.astro";
import QuickPicks from "../components/QuickPicks.astro";
import ProductCard from "../components/ProductCard.astro";
import PlanTheJob from "../components/PlanTheJob.astro";
import AuthorBio from "../components/AuthorBio.astro";
import { amazonLink } from "../data/affiliate";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";
import productImages from "../data/product-images.json";
import { pageDates } from "../data/dates";

const moreInCategory = [
  {
    "title": "Zero-Turn Mowers for Big Lawns",
    "url": "/best-zero-turn-mower/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Riding Mowers for 1 to 3 Acres",
    "url": "/best-riding-lawn-mower/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Self-Propelled Mowers for Slopes",
    "url": "/best-self-propelled-lawn-mower/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Log Splitters",
    "url": "/best-log-splitter/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Chainsaws",
    "url": "/best-chainsaw/"
  }
];
const dates = pageDates(Astro.url.pathname, { published: "2026-11-02", modified: "2026-11-02" });
const title = "6 Best Compact Tractors (2026): Ranked by Weight and Hitch";
const description =
  "The Kubota BX23S leads 6 compact tractors; sub-compacts with a loader run about $18,000 to $30,000, compacts $25,000 to $45,000. Sized for 2 to 20 acres.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    "id": "kubota-bx23s",
    "name": "Kubota BX23S Sub-Compact TLB",
    "category": "TLB Package | Loader + Backhoe",
    "badge": "Best Overall",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Comes as a tractor, loader and backhoe package",
      "Quick-attach backhoe removes without tools",
      "Kubota diesel and hydrostatic drive with a strong reputation",
      "4WD standard",
      "Excellent resale value"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Sub-compact size limits heavy loader work",
      "Package price is high for buyers who do not need a backhoe"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The best all-round small-property tractor if digging is on your list of jobs.",
    "description": "The BX23S is a sub-compact tractor sold as a complete tractor-loader-backhoe package, and that is the reason it leads this list. For a property owner with trenches to dig, stumps to remove, drainage to install or small ponds to shape, a backhoe that comes with the tractor and comes off quickly is a major advantage. Kubota designed the backhoe to attach and detach without tools, so you can switch to mowing or snow work without spending an afternoon on it. The tractor uses a Kubota diesel and a hydrostatic transmission with 4WD standard. Owners commonly praise how capable it is for its size. The limits are the limits of every sub-compact: it is a light machine, so heavy loader work and large implements are beyond it, and you need rear ballast or the backhoe mounted when using the loader. If you do not need a backhoe, the package price is hard to justify, and a non-TLB sub-compact makes more sense."
  },
  {
    "id": "john-deere-1025r",
    "name": "John Deere 1025R",
    "category": "Mower-First | Drive-Over Deck",
    "badge": "Best Dealer Support",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "AutoConnect drive-over mid-mount mower deck",
      "Twin Touch hydrostatic pedals",
      "Deere's wide dealer network",
      "Large range of matched implements",
      "Strong resale value"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Higher price than comparable sub-compacts",
      "Light weight limits heavy loader and ground work"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The easiest sub-compact to own if mowing is a weekly job and you value a nearby dealer.",
    "description": "The 1025R is one of the most popular sub-compact tractors, and much of that comes from how well it integrates with mowing. Deere's AutoConnect deck lets you drive over a mid-mount mower deck and attach it without tools, which matters if the tractor mows every week and does loader or snow work in between. The Twin Touch hydrostatic pedals, one for forward and one for reverse, make loader work and mowing easy to learn. Deere's dealer network is broad in many regions, and the company offers a large range of matched loaders, backhoes, snow blowers and three-point implements. Owners commonly mention strong resale value. The trade-offs are price, which is usually higher than comparable Kioti, LS or Massey models, and the inherent limits of a sub-compact: it is light, so heavy loader work and larger implements are better suited to a compact tractor. For buyers who want a mower-first tractor with good support, it is a safe choice."
  },
  {
    "id": "kioti-cs2520",
    "name": "Kioti CS2520",
    "category": "Value Pick | Long Warranty",
    "badge": "Best Warranty",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Typically priced below Deere and Kubota equivalents",
      "Kioti warranty terms are often longer than rivals",
      "Diesel engine and hydrostatic drive",
      "Loader and mid-mount mower options",
      "Solid build for its class"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Dealer network thinner in some regions",
      "Resale value lower than Deere or Kubota"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "More warranty and equipment per dollar, if a Kioti dealer is within reasonable distance.",
    "description": "Kioti's CS2520 is a sub-compact that competes directly with the Deere 1025R and Kubota BX series, usually at a lower price. Kioti has built a reputation for offering warranty coverage that is often longer than rivals, though terms change, so confirm the current warranty with a dealer. The tractor uses a diesel engine and a hydrostatic transmission, and it can be equipped with a front loader and mid-mount mower deck. Owners commonly describe it as solid and capable for typical small-property work: mowing, light loader work, moving mulch and gravel, and snow clearing with the right attachment. The main consideration is the dealer. Kioti's network is growing but is thinner than Deere or Kubota in some regions, and resale value is typically lower. If a Kioti dealer is nearby and has a good service reputation, the CS2520 offers strong value."
  },
  {
    "id": "kubota-l2502",
    "name": "Kubota L2502",
    "category": "Full Compact | Heavier Frame",
    "badge": "Best for Larger Acreage",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Heavier compact frame handles more serious loader and ground work",
      "Category 1 three-point hitch runs a wider range of implements",
      "Available with gear or hydrostatic transmission",
      "Kubota diesel reliability",
      "Strong resale value"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Larger size is less nimble on small lawns",
      "No mid-mount mower option on many configurations"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The step up when your property has more ground work than mowing.",
    "description": "The L2502 is a true compact tractor rather than a sub-compact, and the difference shows in weight and capability. It is a heavier machine with a Category 1 three-point hitch that runs a wide range of standard implements, including box blades, rotary tillers, post-hole diggers and rotary cutters sized for real field work. That makes it a better fit for properties of five to twenty acres with pasture to brush-hog, driveways to grade, gardens to till and firewood to haul. Kubota offers it with gear or hydrostatic transmissions, and owners commonly praise its durability. The trade-offs are size and mowing. It is less nimble around a house and lawn than a sub-compact, and many configurations do not offer a mid-mount mower, so lawn mowing may need a separate mower. If your property's work is mostly field and ground engagement, the L2502 is worth the step up."
  },
  {
    "id": "massey-ferguson-gc1725m",
    "name": "Massey Ferguson GC1725M",
    "category": "Smooth HST | Comfortable Station",
    "badge": "Best Hydrostatic Feel",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Smooth hydrostatic transmission",
      "Comfortable operator station",
      "Loader and mower deck options",
      "Competitive pricing",
      "Massey Ferguson dealer support"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Dealer network varies by region",
      "Fewer matched implements than Deere"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A comfortable, smooth sub-compact for mowing and light loader work.",
    "description": "The GC1725M is Massey Ferguson's sub-compact, and owners commonly comment on how smooth its hydrostatic transmission feels, which makes it pleasant for loader work and mowing. It can be equipped with a front loader and a mid-mount mower deck, covering the core jobs of a small-property tractor. The operator station is comfortable for its size, and pricing is competitive with Kioti and LS. Massey Ferguson dealers are often agricultural dealerships, which can be a plus for parts and service if one is nearby. As with other non-Deere, non-Kubota brands, the dealer network varies by region, and the range of matched implements is smaller than Deere's. Like every sub-compact, it is a light machine best suited to mowing, light loader work and snow clearing rather than heavy ground work. Confirm current specs with a dealer."
  },
  {
    "id": "ls-mt225s",
    "name": "LS MT225S",
    "category": "Budget Diesel | 4WD HST",
    "badge": "Best Budget Pick",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Low price for a diesel sub-compact",
      "Hydrostatic transmission and 4WD",
      "Loader and mower deck options",
      "LS warranty terms are competitive",
      "Simple, straightforward design"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Smaller dealer network",
      "Lower resale value than major brands"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The lowest-cost way into a diesel sub-compact, if service is nearby.",
    "description": "The MT225S is LS Tractor's sub-compact and one of the most affordable diesel sub-compacts from an established brand. It offers a hydrostatic transmission, 4WD and options for a front loader and mid-mount mower deck, covering the main jobs a small property owner needs. LS has offered competitive warranty terms, but confirm the current coverage with a dealer. Owners commonly describe it as a straightforward, capable tractor for the price. The trade-offs are those you would expect from a budget brand: a smaller dealer network, lower resale value and fewer matched implements. If an LS dealer is nearby and you want to keep the budget for implements rather than the tractor itself, it is a sensible choice. If dealer support is limited in your area, the savings may not be worth the service hassle."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Compact Tractor Picks",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-compact-tractor/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which compact tractor fits most small properties?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On a two-to-five-acre property, a sub-compact such as the Kubota BX23S, John Deere 1025R or Kioti CS2520 covers mowing, loader work and snow. Choose the BX23S if you need a backhoe. With five to twenty acres of pasture and heavier ground work, a full compact like the Kubota L2502 is the better match."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "At what acreage does a tractor make sense?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The jobs matter more than the acreage. Owners of two acres or more who regularly move gravel, mulch or soil, grade driveways, brush-hog or clear snow often find a sub-compact worth it. If you mostly mow, a lawn tractor or zero-turn is cheaper and faster. Write down your yearly jobs before you decide."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I choose between sub-compact and compact?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A sub-compact suits smaller properties that need mowing, light loader work and snow clearing, especially where storage is tight. A compact suits larger properties with heavier ground work, bigger implements and more serious loader use. When you are on the fence, many owners advise the larger tractor, and storage space and gate widths often decide it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does a compact tractor cost with implements?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "At the time of writing, a sub-compact with a loader typically costs about $18,000 to $30,000, and a compact with a loader roughly $25,000 to $45,000 or more. A box blade, rotary cutter and rear blade can add several thousand dollars on top. Package deals from the dealer can bring the total down."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I buy a backhoe attachment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A backhoe can pay for itself if you dig regularly, for trenching, stump removal or drainage. For occasional digging, renting a mini excavator or hiring a contractor may cost less. A backhoe also works as rear ballast during loader work. Be honest about how often you would really use it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which tractor brands hold resale value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "John Deere and Kubota usually hold their value well, helped by strong brand recognition and wide dealer networks. Kioti, Massey Ferguson and LS often cost less to buy but typically resell for less. Condition, hours and maintenance records weigh heavily on resale too, and a well-kept tractor of any brand sells more easily."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does a small tractor need four-wheel drive?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most small-property owners, yes. Four-wheel drive adds traction for loader work, slopes, snow and soft ground, and it is the safer choice on slopes. Most sub-compact and compact tractors sold with loaders have 4WD as standard. Two-wheel drive mostly appears on basic models meant for flat, dry mowing and light work."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "All Metal Brake" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Lawn Mowers & Tractors",
    tags: [
      "best compact tractor",
      "sub-compact tractor",
      "tractor loader backhoe",
      "compact tractor implements",
      "hobby farm tractor",
      "tractor for acreage"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <header data-hero class="bg-[#F4F6F8] border-b border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-10 pb-8 lg:pt-14 lg:pb-10">
        <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest m-0 mb-4">
          <span class="text-[#D93A00]">Buyer's Guide</span>
          <span class="text-gray-300" aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Updated {dates.display}</span>
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-[2.1rem] leading-[1.15] sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-gray-900 m-0">
          Best Compact Tractor
        </h1>
        <QuickAnswer products={PRODUCTS} />
        <p class="text-lg lg:text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-5 mb-0">
          The Kubota BX23S is our top compact tractor for 2 to 5 acres, because it arrives as a loader and quick-detach backhoe package with 4WD standard. The heaviest job on your land and the distance to a good dealer can change that, and 5 to 20 acres of ground work points to the Kubota L2502. This guide compares six tractors, size classes, implements, prices and safety.
        </p>
        <!-- Author & Meta -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-7">
          <AuthorAvatar size={40} />
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 m-0">Written by <a href="/authors/alex-rivers/" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Alex Rivers</a></p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 m-0">Home Improvement Editor &middot; Updated {dates.display}</p>
          </div>
          <SocialProof users="" />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-6">
          <TrustBadge />
          <span class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-300"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-0">
          Based on manufacturer specs, hitch category, loader ratings, dealer coverage and owner forum themes. Not hands-on tested. No paid placements. <a href="/how-we-test/" class="font-bold text-gray-900 underline">Read how we pick</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
      <details open class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl px-5 pt-4 pb-2">
        <summary class="flex items-center gap-3 pb-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" d="M9 6h11M9 12h11M9 18h11M4.5 6h.01M4.5 12h.01M4.5 18h.01" /></svg>
          <span class="font-bold text-gray-900">In This Guide</span>
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400">18 sections</span>
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-auto text-gray-500 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 15l6-6 6 6" /></svg>
        </summary>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6">
              <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">1.</span><span>The Short Answer</span></a>
              <a href="#top-picks" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">2.</span><span>The 6 Best Compact Tractors</span></a>
              <a href="#do-you-need" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">3.</span><span>Tractor or Bigger Mower?</span></a>
              <a href="#size-classes" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">4.</span><span>Sub-Compact vs Compact</span></a>
              <a href="#weight" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">5.</span><span>Why Weight Beats Horsepower</span></a>
              <a href="#hitch-pto" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">6.</span><span>Which Hitch and PTO?</span></a>
              <a href="#transmissions" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">7.</span><span>Hydrostatic or Gear?</span></a>
              <a href="#loaders" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">8.</span><span>Choosing a Front Loader</span></a>
              <a href="#backhoes" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">9.</span><span>Is a Backhoe Worth It?</span></a>
              <a href="#implements" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">10.</span><span>Implements and Their Cost</span></a>
              <a href="#snow" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">11.</span><span>Clearing Snow</span></a>
              <a href="#tires" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">12.</span><span>Which Tires?</span></a>
              <a href="#dealer" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">13.</span><span>Choosing a Dealer</span></a>
              <a href="#safety" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">14.</span><span>Operating Safely</span></a>
              <a href="#upkeep" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">15.</span><span>Maintenance</span></a>
              <a href="#budget" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">16.</span><span>What Does One Cost?</span></a>
              <a href="#mistakes" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">17.</span><span>Common Mistakes</span></a>
              <a href="#faq" class="flex items-baseline gap-3 py-2.5 border-t border-gray-100 text-[15px] text-gray-700 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline"><span class="w-6 shrink-0 text-gray-400 font-semibold">18.</span><span>FAQ</span></a>
        </nav>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Most people compare compact tractors on horsepower and brand name. Yet the jobs that count on a few acres, like shifting gravel, grading a driveway, lifting round bales or digging a trench, hinge far more on four other things: the tractor's weight, its three-point hitch category, how much its loader can lift, and how far away the nearest dealer is. Answer those four first and the brand decision largely makes itself.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <!-- Short Answer -->
        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Best Compact Tractor: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            On two to five acres, a sub-compact handles mowing, loader work and snow, and the Kubota BX23S leads because its backhoe comes in the package and detaches without tools. Choose the John Deere 1025R if weekly mowing and a nearby dealer matter most, or the Kioti CS2520 for more warranty per dollar. With five to twenty acres of pasture and ground work, step up to the full-compact Kubota L2502. Whatever you pick, confirm current specs with a dealer.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Tractor</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Size Class</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best For</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Deciding Feature</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
