        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Begin with the heaviest job your land demands, then pick the size class, weight and hitch category that can handle it. On most two-to-five-acre properties a sub-compact such as the Kubota BX23S, John Deere 1025R or Kioti CS2520 is the right machine, and the BX23S wins if digging is part of the plan. Larger properties with pasture and heavier work call for a full compact like the Kubota L2502.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Vet the dealer as closely as the tractor, put implements in the budget from day one, and stick to the basic safety habits: ROPS raised, seat belt fastened, ballast on the back and loads kept low. Chosen well, a compact tractor will work your land for decades.
          </p>
